course: dictionary
lesson: 1224
title: Bulk: most, size, and in bulk
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it tell you which one you need. «The bulk of the work was finished by lunchtime.» Here bulk means most of the work, because finished by lunchtime tells you the job was nearly all done.
explain: «The elephant's huge bulk made the bridge creak.» Huge is a clue. Bulk means the large size and weight of the elephant. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: «Buy rice in bulk» means buy large amounts at once. The phrase in bulk is about quantity, and it usually means each item costs less. Bulk up is a different use: it is a verb meaning to get bigger, often by gaining muscle.
fact: «Bulk» can mean most of something: «the bulk of the work».
fact: «Bulk» can mean the large size or weight of something: «the elephant's huge bulk».
fact: «In bulk» means in large amounts, usually at a lower price for each item.
fact: Buying in bulk saves money only on things that last and get used, like rice and pasta, not on food that goes off.
fact: «Bulk up» means to get bigger, often by gaining muscle.
exercise: «The bulk of the work was finished by lunchtime.» What does bulk mean here? | A heavy box | A loud noise | A tiny part of the work | *Most of the work
exercise: Mum says, «Buy rice in bulk, it is cheaper.» What does in bulk mean? | In the bulk bin at the back | *In large amounts, usually cheaper for each item | Without paying | In small packets only
exercise: «The elephant's huge bulk made the bridge creak.» What does bulk mean here? | A cheap price | *Its large size and weight | A small sound | A fast run
test: A 5kg bag of rice costs £5. Five 1kg bags cost £1.50 each. How much do you save by buying in bulk? | £7.50 | *£2.50 | £1.50 | £5.00
test: Which things are best to buy in bulk? | Fresh fish that goes off quickly | Soft fruit that goes mouldy in days | Milk that turns sour by Friday | *Rice and pasta that last and get used
exam: Someone offers you something to «bulk up» quickly. What should you do? | *Say no and tell an adult | Take it home quietly and try it | Keep it secret from everyone | Accept it, since bulking up is always good
